<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajendra Prasad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1884">1884</a>–<a href="/years/1963">1963</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajendra Prasad was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a> leader and lawyer from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> who became the first President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, serving from 1950 to 1962. A close associate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Mahatma Gandhi</a> from the Champaran campaign of 1917 and a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a>, he presided over the Constituent Assembly that drafted the constitution. He is the only Indian president to have served two full terms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajendra-prasad.jpg" alt="Rajendra Prasad" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archives New Zealand from New Zealand · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rajendra_Prasad_(Indian_President),_signed_image_for_Walter_Nash_(NZ_Prime_Minister),_1958_(16017609534).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
